            "n_events": 25,
            "result_text": "Done! The function uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrency. When you press Ctrl+C:\n\n1. It cancels all pending tasks\n2. Waits for them to finish with `return_exceptions=True` so the CancelledError doesn't prevent other tasks from cleaning up\n3. This allows any `try/finally` blocks or async context managers in your tasks to run their cleanup code\n4. Then re-raises the KeyboardInterrupt\n\nYou can now use it like:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        await asyncio.sleep(10)\n    finally:\n        print(\"Cleaning up!\")\n\nasyncio.run(run_tasks([my_task], max_concurrent=5))\n```"
        }
